          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mtqsx7zbpuaiqgzo",
          "message": {
            "text": "The browser regression first inspects the actual DOM/CSS geometry, then proves capture anchors follow the 120 px element scrollport instead of the 260 px outer frame. Before the fix it failed with [0, 260, 360]; after the chunk-size decision (0) it records [0, 120, 240, 360], so every moving slice is contiguous.",
            "markdown": "The browser regression first inspects the actual DOM/CSS geometry, then proves capture anchors follow the 120 px element scrollport instead of the 260 px outer frame. Before the fix it failed with [0, 260, 360]; after the [chunk-size decision](0) it records [0, 120, 240, 360], so every moving slice is contiguous."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tests/scroll-inner-live.e2e.test.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 74,
                  "endLine": 101,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  it(\"chunks a long element-owned scroll by the element scrollport\", async () => {\n    const page = await env!.browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 360, height: 260 } });\n    try {\n      await page.setContent(`<!doctype html><style>\n        body{margin:0}#list{width:260px;height:120px;overflow:auto}.row{box-sizing:border-box;height:40px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd}\n      </style><div id=\"list\">${Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, i) => `<div class=\"row\">ROW ${i}</div>`).join(\"\")}</div>`);\n\n      // Inspect the live layout that governs each captured slice. The owner is\n      // shorter than the outer capture frame, which is the seam-producing case.\n      expect(await page.locator(\"#list\").evaluate((element) => {\n        const style = getComputedStyle(element);\n        return {\n          clientHeight: element.clientHeight,\n          scrollHeight: element.scrollHeight,\n          overflowY: style.overflowY,\n        };\n      })).toEqual({ clientHeight: 120, scrollHeight: 480, overflowY: \"auto\" });\n\n      const segments = await executeScrollPattern(page, parseScrollPattern(\"down:bottom/400ms\"), {\n        selector: \"#list\",\n        captureSelector: \"body\",\n        captureViewport: { x: 0, y: 0, width: 360, height: 260 },\n        viewportW: 360,\n        viewportH: 260,\n        prescroll: false,\n      });\n\n      expect(segments.map((segment) => segment.scrollY)).toEqual([0, 120, 240, 360]);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "test-evidence"
            ],
            "ext-ai-tool-confidence": 1
          },
